    ("Con", "Let me play back what I'd put in a first version, just so you can hear it, not to sign anything. One. A job board, one row per job, from won quote to invoiced, with the stages you use, proofing, production, ready, installed, invoiced. Both sites on it, with a site column, so Flint has its own view of the same thing rather than its own copy. Two. The proof and its approval on the job, so the floor sees the signed version and only the signed version, and a change after sign-off is a visible change, not a reply in someone's inbox. Three. The ticket printed from the job, so it reprints when the job changes. Four. Install scheduling for the six crews, off the same jobs, so a job that's gone back into paint can't show as ready. Five. An installed flag that tells Bronwyn, so the invoice follows the install and not the Friday walk. Quoting stays in the estimating tool and the job number keeps coming from the accounting system. Is that the right shape?", "con_scope_playback"),
    ("Del", "That's the right shape. Two things. Don't build the quoting in it, ever, Fergus will never forgive me. The estimating tool stays. And the job number has to come from the accounting system, we're not typing that twice either.", "del_scope_agree"),
